                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.29677/2610.29677v1/figures/art_retain.png",
                "caption": "Figure 9:A proposed test of the two links of recursive self-improvement (R1 and R2).In R2, the updated improver revises itself with frozen or acquired knowledge, producing the control or next improver, respectively. Each then revises a learning procedure, which is tested through fresh matched learners under a common, protected outcome check; the next improver must beat both the control and the updated improver; for the updated improver, its learner from R1 serves as the baseline. The R2 control assumes that the acquired knowledge can be withheld without changing the parent improver, as with a memory snapshot; the count of four hardware-trained learners per seed assumes that one candidate per improver survives screening.",
                "position": 4194
            },
